WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.340
[gentle music]

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.940
A marketplace of chiplets presents
opportunities and challenges.

3
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.960
In previous modules,

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.520
you've learned of opportunities
like reusing proven chiplets,

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.560
mixing different process nodes,
and reducing development time and costs,

6
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.580
as well as challenges such as the need
for high-speed die-to-die interfaces,

7
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.000
interoperability between
different vendors' chiplets,

8
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:34.100
and the complexities and costs associated
with advanced packaging and testability.

9
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.830
A marketplace of chiplets is
based on the emerging chiplet

10
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:42.980
paradigm shift away from
traditional monolithic chip design,

11
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.040
where a single complex
chip serves all functions,

12
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.700
toward a more flexible
mix-and-match approach.

13
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.810
In this course, we'll look at
opportunities and challenges

14
00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.220
in turn and what role
the marketplace is serving.

15
00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.840
Let's start with the opportunities.

16
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.439
First, chiplets enable cost efficiency.

17
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.960
Companies can design
and manufacture smaller,

18
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.160
specialized components
rather than expensive,

19
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.260
large-scale chips, reducing
production costs and risks.

20
00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:20.510
This creates more marketplace
diversity by creating

21
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.140
a role for the chiplet creator
and a role for the assembler,

22
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.540
as well as other nuanced roles
in between and downstream.

23
00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.360
This modularity also
accelerates innovation,

24
00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.080
as firms can swap or upgrade
individual chiplets,

25
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.460
such as for AI memory or I/O,

26
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.120
without redesigning an entire
system on chip, or SoC.

27
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.940
This means that a company could
pair a high-performance CPU chiplet

28
00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.020
with a tailored GPU chiplet
to meet specific needs,

29
00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.300
fostering rapid
prototyping and deployment.

30
00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:02.110
Additionally, a marketplace democratizes
access, allowing smaller players

31
00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.900
to compete by sourcing chiplets rather
than designing all chiplets on their own,

32
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.880
a significant advantage amid soaring
fabrication costs, where, for example,

33
00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.740
TSMC's advanced nodes cost
millions to tape out in.

34
00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.440
Finally, sustainability also benefits,

35
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:26.800
as reusable chiplets reduce waste
compared to discarding entire SoCs.

36
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.560
Now let's turn to challenges.

37
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.980
This model introduces complexity.

38
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.080
Interoperability is a major hurdle.

39
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.000
Chiplets from different vendors
must communicate seamlessly,

40
00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.700
requiring standardized interfaces,
as discussed in module four.

41
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.460
Without robust standards,
integration could falter,

42
00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.180
leading to performance
bottlenecks or incompatibility.

43
00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.520
Quality control poses another issue.

44
00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.880
A single defective chiplet could
compromise an entire system.

45
00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.170
Yet testing modular
components across a supply

46
00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.700
chain is trickier than
vetting a monolithic chip.

47
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.980
Intellectual property and security
risks are also a concern.

48
00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.770
Vendors may hesitate to share
proprietary designs, and combining

49
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.300
chiplets could expose vulnerabilities
if not tightly coordinated.

50
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.880
Finally, the marketplace demands a mature
ecosystem, including reliable suppliers,

51
00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.680
clear pricing, and trust,
which is still developing.

52
00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.690
In a sense, a chiplet
marketplace promises innovation

53
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:41.080
and accessibility but hinges on
solving technical, logistical,

54
00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:46.060
and economic challenges to truly
disrupt the semiconductor landscape.

55
00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.260
In the OCP community,

56
00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.820
The Open Chiplet Economy Project is
committed to facilitating that work,

57
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.710
and the OCP's multi-vendor
open marketplace

58
00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.400
has a dedicated section for chiplets, too,

59
00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:04.860
including everything from technical and
business tools and components to design,

60
00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.420
assemble, test, and package chiplets.

61
00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:13.220
[gentle music]

